PhotoCraft is an open-source, native image editor written in Rust,
with familiar professional tools: layers, masks, adjustment layers,
layer styles, type and brushes. It opens and saves layered PSD/PSB
files, works on 8/16/32-bit documents and composites on the GPU via
wgpu. The package also ships photocraft-cli, a headless converter and
command runner.

This package repacks the upstream prebuilt x86_64 binary. It needs
glibc 2.35 or newer, so it runs on Slackware -current, not 15.0.

Window-system and GPU libraries (X11/xcb, libxkbcommon, wayland,
Vulkan or EGL) are loaded at runtime and are all part of a full
Slackware install.

Upstream marks PhotoCraft as early alpha.
